  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 129 AM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nUpper level ridge builds into the area today which will remove \nthe trigger for organized thunderstorms this afternoon. However,\ndeep monsoonal moisture remains in place today. Expect isolated\nto scattered thunderstorms to develop mainly across the \nmountains and highlands this afternoon. The high res models are \npicking up on this as well. Some gusty winds and brief heavy \ndownpours will remain possible with these storms. Most of this \nactivity should diminish this evening with the loss of the \nafternoon heating. But, we will likely see a repeat performance \nfor Monday. \n\nA shortwave trough will move over the top of the ridge through \nMontana Monday night into Tuesday. Models are showing that this \ntrough may help to enhance shower and thunderstorm chance during \nthat time. \n\nThe upper level flow switches to northwesterly with the ridge \namplifying just to our west. This may help dry us out and reduce the \nthunderstorm chances for the second half of the week.\n\nTemperatures will begin to warm up. Still slightly below normal for \nthe first half of the week, but then increasing to slightly above \nnormal for the second half of the week as the ridge amplifies.",
